---
/* THE LETTERS, PUBLISHED AS DRAFTS.
 *
 * Four letters were sitting in requests/ unpublished, one of them since
 * September. A draft nobody finds is a question nobody asks, and every one of
 * these is a gap this atlas cannot close by reading — because the data is not
 * published, because the server is down, or because the archive has said no to
 * crawlers and a letter is the honest remaining channel.
 *
 * The text is read from requests/ by scripts/build-errands.py and never
 * retyped, so this page cannot drift from the files. Nothing here sends
 * anything.
 */
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Errands from "../components/Errands.astro";
import { u } from "../lib/url.js";
import errands from "../data/errands.json";

const c = errands.counts;
---
{/* `title` WITHOUT THE SITE NAME AND NO <h1> HERE. Base.astro renders
    «{title} — {site.name}» into the document title and prints {title} as the
    page's own h1, so this page first shipped «Errands — Record Atlas — Record
    Atlas» with two h1 elements on it. The convention every other page follows
    is title/eyebrow/dek as props and no heading in the body. */}
<Base
  noindex
  title="Errands"
  eyebrow={`${c.letters} letters · ${c.drafted} drafted and unsent`}
  dek="Some gaps cannot be closed by reading: the data is not published, the server is down, or the archive has told crawlers no. The honest move is to ask a person."
  description="Letters this atlas has drafted to close the gaps reading cannot: the exact words, and which of them have gone.">
  {/* The count is in the eyebrow; repeating it here was the same sentence twice. */}
  <ul class="k-pills er-pills" aria-label="Summary">
    <li><span class="k-pill"><b>{c.letters}</b> letters</span></li>
    <li><span class="k-pill is-solid">{c.drafted} drafted, unsent</span></li>
  </ul>
  <div class="k-hi er-hi">
    <p>Sending one is David's decision, always, and the date it went is recorded beside it afterwards.</p>
    <p>The text is read from <code>requests/</code> in the repository and never retyped here, so what you read is what was sent.</p>
  </div>
  <Errands groups={errands.groups} u={u} />
  <aside class="k-foot">
    <p>Why these and not others?</p>
    <p>This atlas does not work around a bot gate, and it does not read a sibling host to get what a named host refused. Where that leaves a question unanswered, the question goes here instead of quietly disappearing. See <a href={u("/worklist/")}>what is still missing</a>.</p>
  </aside>
</Base>

<style is:global>
  .er-pills { margin: 0 0 18px; }
  .er-pills .k-pill { font-size: 14px; padding: 6px 14px; }
  main .er-hi { max-width: none; border-radius: 18px; }
  main .er .er-g { margin-top: 26px; }
  main .er .er-lab { font: 800 clamp(22px, 3vw, 28px)/1.2 var(--serif); letter-spacing: -.02em; display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; gap: 4px 12px; }
  main .er .er-lab::before { content: ""; flex: none; width: 8px; height: 28px; border-radius: 6px; background: var(--hue); }
  main .er .er-row { max-width: none; border-radius: 18px; border-top: 5px solid var(--hue); }
  main .er .er-row h3 { font-weight: 800; letter-spacing: -.01em; }
  main .er .er-n { font-weight: 700; }
  main .er .er-draft summary { color: var(--hue-ink); }
  /* the tag's colour comes from the row as an inline style (a state colour that is 2.6:1 on the dark panel); the words say the state, so it takes the page's own ink */
  main .er .er-tag { color: var(--hue-ink) !important; border-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--hue) 55%, transparent) !important; }
  main .k-foot { max-width: none; border-radius: 18px; }
</style>
